verses.raw_usfm:
but the idol made with hands is accursed, itself and he that made it;  
\q2 because his was the working, and the corruptible thing was called a god.   
\q1

But worship was raised to a yet higher pitch, even by those who didn’t know him,  
\q2 urged forward by the ambition of the architect;   
\q1

for he, wishing perhaps to please his ruler,  
\q2 used his art to force the likeness toward a greater beauty.   
\q1
